# Environment for the administrative surface.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is the
# committed template and must never contain real values.
#
# The public site needs NONE of these. It builds and serves with this file
# absent, reading journal essays from content/journal/articles.ts. Everything
# below exists so that /admin can run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (required for /admin, and for journal editing to persist)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any Postgres 14+ connection string. Managed Postgres on Vercel, Neon and
# Supabase all work; all three require TLS, hence `sslmode=require`.
#
# Once set, the public journal reads from the database instead of the bundled
# content module. Apply the schema and copy the bundled essays across with:
#   npm run db:migrate
#   npm run db:seed
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing (required for /admin)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs session cookies and hashes IP addresses in the audit log. Minimum 32
# characters. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Rotating this invalidates every live session — the intended response to a
# suspected token leak.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WebAuthn relying party (required for /admin)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMIN_RP_ID is the bare registrable domain: no scheme, no port, no path and no
# subdomain. For this site that is `restoreeuropa.eu` — NOT `www.restoreeuropa.eu`,
# which would bind credentials to the www host and leave them unusable on the apex.
# ADMIN_ORIGIN is the exact origin the browser will see, scheme included.
#
# A passkey is cryptographically bound to these values, so changing either one
# orphans every credential already enrolled. For local development use
# `localhost` and `http://localhost:3000` — the only origin browsers exempt from
# the HTTPS requirement.
#
# In production:
#   ADMIN_RP_ID=restoreeuropa.eu
#   ADMIN_ORIGIN=https://restoreeuropa.eu
ADMIN_RP_ID=localhost
ADMIN_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# First-passkey enrolment (required once, then inert)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Permits the very first passkey to be enrolled at /admin/enrol. Honoured only
# while no credential exists; after that it does nothing and further passkeys
# can be added only from an authenticated session. Generate as above.
ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Membership encryption (required for /admin/members)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encrypts members' names and email addresses at rest. 32 bytes, base64url.
# Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Two rules, and they pull in opposite directions:
#
#   1. NEVER store or back this up alongside the database it protects. The whole
#      point is that a stolen dump decrypts to nothing; a dump that travels with
#      its key is just a slower plaintext.
#   2. NEVER lose it. There is no recovery path — losing this key destroys every
#      membership record irreversibly. Keep a backup somewhere the database
#      backups are not, such as a password manager or paper in a safe.
#
# Without it, /admin/members explains that it is unset and refuses to read or
# write membership records. The public site is unaffected either way: it collects
# nothing, so it never touches this key.
MEMBER_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel Web Analytics (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read-only figures for the dashboard. Without these the dashboard reports that
# the source is not connected rather than inventing numbers — collection still
# works, only the admin read-back is disabled.
#
# The token needs the Read scope for the project. VERCEL_TEAM_ID is required
# only for projects owned by a team rather than a personal account.
VERCEL_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
